# kunkeconsulting.com, registered 2026-08-06 at Porkbun as a defensive catch. The
# .pl stays the only public address; the .com exists to hand its visitors over.
# Netlify auto-redirects a domain's own apex to its own www and back, but never
# between two different domains, so this pair has to be spelled out. Path-
# preserving, so a .com link to any page lands on the same page on the .pl.
#
# These rules are inert until two things are true: the .com is attached to this
# Netlify site as a domain alias, and Porkbun's DNS points at Netlify. Until then
# they match nothing. Host-scoped, so they cannot affect kunkeconsulting.pl.
http://kunkeconsulting.com/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!
https://kunkeconsulting.com/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!
http://www.kunkeconsulting.com/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!
https://www.kunkeconsulting.com/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!

# Netlify serves every site at its own <site>.netlify.app address as well as at
# the custom domain, so the entire site was also live and crawlable at
# kunkeconsulting.netlify.app. Its pages canonical back to the .pl, so Google
# was not indexing them, but a second public copy of the site is worth closing
# off. Deploy previews use deploy-preview-N--kunkeconsulting.netlify.app, a
# different host, so they are unaffected.
http://kunkeconsulting.netlify.app/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!
https://kunkeconsulting.netlify.app/*  https://kunkeconsulting.pl/:splat  301!

/sitemap.xml  /sitemap-index.xml  301!
/new  /  301!
/new/  /  301!
